.TH IMUD\-SIGNALK 8 "July 2026" "imud 1.1" "System Manager's Manual"
.SH NAME
imud\-signalk \- bridge imud's binary stream to Signal K over UDP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B imud-signalk
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B imud-signalk
connects to the local AF_UNIX binary subscription stream published by
.BR imud (8)
and emits Signal K
.I delta
messages (JSON) over UDP for every value imud produces that has a standard
Signal K path.  Signal K did not reliably parse all of imud's NMEA 0183 output;
this bridge feeds Signal K natively instead, while the NMEA output is left
unchanged.
.PP
The bridge holds no hardware.  It reconnects automatically if
.BR imud (8)
restarts.  It reads the stream socket named by its own
.B socket
key (default
.IR /run/imud/imud-stream.sock ),
so
.BR imud (8)
must have its
.B [stream]
output enabled.
.PP
All values use Signal K SI units (radians, rad/s, metres).  The fields emitted
are:
.PP
.RS 4
.TS
l l.
navigation.headingMagnetic	always
navigation.headingTrue	when declination is known
navigation.magneticVariation	when declination is known
navigation.rateOfTurn	always
navigation.attitude	roll, pitch, yaw (always)
environment.heave	when publish_heave is set
.TE
.RE
.PP
One delta is sent per UDP datagram at the configured rate (default 10 Hz),
timestamped from the packet's wall-clock time.  Configure a matching UDP
connection on the Signal K server (Server \(-> Connections \(-> Add, type UDP)
listening on the bridge's destination port.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config \ PATH
Load configuration from
.I PATH
instead of
.IR /etc/imud/imud-signalk.conf .
Only the
.B [imud-signalk]
section is read.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Reload the configuration.  The emit rate, destination address/port, source
label, heave publishing, and log level are applied live; if the reload fails to
parse, the running configuration is kept.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Graceful shutdown.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The bridge reads its own file (default
.IR /etc/imud/imud-signalk.conf ),
using only the
.B [imud-signalk]
section:
.TP
.B enabled
Start the bridge (also gate with the systemd unit).  [restart]
.TP
.B socket
imud stream socket to read (default
.IR /run/imud/imud-stream.sock ).  [restart]
.TP
.BR dest_addr ", " dest_port
Signal K server host and UDP input port (default 127.0.0.1:10113).  [hot]
.TP
.B rate_hz
Delta emit rate (default 10).  [hot]
.TP
.B source_label
Signal K delta
.B source.label
(default "imud").  [hot]
.TP
.B publish_heave
Emit
.B environment.heave
(default true; set false if imud's heave estimator is off).  [hot]
.SH EXAMPLES
Run in the foreground against a local config:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
imud-signalk --config /etc/imud/imud-signalk.conf
.EE
.RE
.PP
Enable as a service (after enabling imud's
.B [stream]
output and
.B enabled
in
.IR imud-signalk.conf ):
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl enable --now imud-signalk
.EE
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/imud/imud-signalk.conf
Default configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR imud (8),
.BR imud.conf (5),
.BR imud-mon (1),
.BR imud-status (1)
